This directory contains the LZMA SDK code used in building the self-extracting
Windows installer.

The src/ directory contains an almost-unmodified copy of the 7-zip source code
version 24.09, as downloaded from https://www.7-zip.org/a/lzma2409.7z (linked
from https://www.7-zip.org/sdk.html) on January 21, 2026. As stated in
DOC/lzma-sdk.txt and on the web page, this code is in the public domain. A few
modifications have been made to this copy of the source code. Those
modifications are contained in mozilla_customizations.diff, which should be
found in the same directory as this file.

The firefox/ directory contains several things:
* SFXSetup.sln and SFXSetup.vcxproj
  These are Visual Studio 2026 conversions of the Visual C++ 6 workspace and
  project files from the src/CPP/7zip/Bundles/SFXSetup/ directory, with
  some changes and additions to support AArch64 and to include our resources.
* 7zSD.arm64.manifest and 7zSD.win32.manifest
  We need to add a manifest file to the binary for several reasons, and one
  isn't supplied with the source package (Visual C++ 6 doesn't support them),
  so we've written our own.
* setup.ico
  The icon group used for the installer package.
* resource.rc
  The resource script containing the above manifest and icon references, as
  well as other resources we need. This is derived from the supplied SFXSetup
  resource.rc, but heavily customized.
* 7zSD.ARM64.sfx
  AArch64 binary built using all the above files. Checking this into the tree in
  compiled binary form means that packaging the installer does not require
  having a compiler toolchain configured (which is the case for artifact
  builds). To compile your own version of this file, open SFXSetup.sln and build
  the ReleaseD configuration.
* 7zSD.Win32.sfx
  32-bit x86 binary built using some of the above files. Checking this into the
  tree in compiled binary form means that packaging the installer does not
  require having a compiler toolchain configured (which is the case for artifact
  builds). To compile your own version of this file, open SFXSetup.sln and build
  the ReleaseD configuration.

Making Future src Customizations
--------------------------------

When we make future customizations, they should be made both to the source
files, and to `mozilla_customizations.diff`. Ideally, this should be done in a
consistent way so that the changes to `mozilla_customizations.diff` are at
least somewhat readable in code review rather than just being a complete
rewrite of the file every time. Following these steps should accomplish this.

  1) Start with a clean copy of firefox's main branch.
  2) Create a new branch `git checkout -b lzma2409-orig`.
  3) Download a copy of the LZMA SDK. If this is no longer available from the
     original 7-zip.org download URL given above, it is available on
     [SourceForge](https://sourceforge.net/projects/sevenzip/files/LZMA%20SDK/lzma2409.7z/download).
  4) The downloaded archive will contain 7 directories. 7 directories with
     matching names are located in `other-licenses\7zstub\src`. Recursively copy
     the extracted directories, overwriting all files.
  5) Commit these files `git commit -a -m "original lzma2409"`
  6) Checkout the main branch again `git checkout main`
  7) Generate a diff and check that it matches `mozilla_customizations.diff`:
     `git diff lzma2409-orig > tmp.diff`

     You will need to remove git's extended header information by hand - see the
     section Removing the Extended Header below for more details.

     After the extended header has been removed you can check if the files are
     the same with `cmp tmp.diff mozilla_customizations.diff`
  8) Make the new customizations.
  9) Build the new `7zSD.ARM64.sfx` and `7zSD.Win32.sfx`.
     This may require that the Visual Studio Installer be re-run to add the
     ARM64 toolchain, if you don't already have it. The current latest is called
     "MSVC v145 - VS 2026 C++ ARM64/ARM64EC build tools (latest)".
     Once the necessary tools are available, open SFXSetup.sln.
     It may ask if you want to use the latest toolset versions rather than the
     ones specified by the project, which should be fine.
     Select the "ReleaseD" solution configuration and the "ARM64" platform and
     build in order to build `7zSD.ARM64.sfx`. Then select the "x86" platform
     and build again to get `7zSD.Win32.sfx`.
  10) Move the new binaries into place and delete the other build files that we
     do not need.
     ```
     mv other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/Win32/ReleaseD/7zSD.Win32.sfx other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/
     mv other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/ARM64/ReleaseD/7zSD.ARM64.sfx other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/
     rm -rf other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/ARM64/
     rm -rf other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/Win32/
     ```
  11) Regenerate `mozilla_customizations.diff`:
      `git diff lzma2409-orig > mozilla_customizations.diff`
  12) Remove any of the extended header information in the diff before committing.

Updating the Version of LZMA
----------------------------

The version of LZMA can be updated in the future with the following procedure.

  1) Copy the new lzma source code folder into the 7zstub folder as `src` replacing what
     is there currently.
  2) Commit the changes
  2) Apply the `mozilla_customizations.diff` patch with
     `patch -p3 < mozilla_customizations.diff`
  3) Open `firefox/SFXSetup.sln` in Visual Studio 2026.
  4) Look at the changes made to `src/CPP/7zip/Bundles/SFXSetup/makefile`
     `git diff src/CPP/7zip/Bundles/SFXSetup/makefile`

     This will show any preprocessor define statements that have changed and any
     files that need added or removed from the Visual Studio project.

     When changing the defines, remember to change them for both build configurations
     `ReleaseD` and `Debug` in each architecture: `Win32` and `ARM64`.

     When adding a C file to the project, you also need to turn off the precompiled
     header support for it in the file's properties, again for both build
     configurations in each architecture.
  5) Build the solution and fix any compilation errors that might have arisen from
     the Mozilla changes due to API changes between LZMA versions.
  6) Once the solution builds correctly, error and warning free, build the
     `ReleaseD` version for both `Win32` and `ARM64`.
  7) Generate the new `mozilla_customizations.diff`
     `git diff > mozilla_customizations.diff` remembering to remove the extended
     headers from the diff file.
  8) Commit the changes in `src`.
  9) Commit the changes to `mozilla_customizations.diff`
  10) Move the new binaries into place and delete the other build files that we
     do not need.
     ```
     mv other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/Win32/ReleaseD/7zSD.Win32.sfx other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/
     mv other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/ARM64/ReleaseD/7zSD.ARM64.sfx other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/
     rm -rf other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/ARM64/
     rm -rf other-licenses/7zstub/firefox/Win32/
     ```
  11) Commit the new binaries.

