Removing the Extended Header
----------------------------

Git diff adds an extended header to each file in the diff that isn't needed for
patching, and could change over time making the resulting PR bigger than necesary.
To avoid this we remove the extended header from the diff file before committing.

The extended header is the lines between the `diff --git a/...` line and the
next `--- a/...` line. Any line between those should be removed. In the example below
the `index 900361e2fcf2..62208804bab0 100644` is the extended header.

```
diff --git a/other-licenses/7zstub/src/CPP/7zip/Bundles/SFXSetup/SFXSetup.dsp b/other-licenses/7zstub/src/CPP/7zip/Bundles/SFXSetup/SFXSetup.dsp
index 900361e2fcf2..62208804bab0 100644
--- a/other-licenses/7zstub/src/CPP/7zip/Bundles/SFXSetup/SFXSetup.dsp
+++ b/other-licenses/7zstub/src/CPP/7zip/Bundles/SFXSetup/SFXSetup.dsp
```